Relevant columns and their potential usage for this task  
• SALES_INVOICES."InvoiceDate": selects invoices that belong to the 2014 calendar year; also used to derive months (SUBSTR("InvoiceDate",1,7)).  
• SALES_INVOICES."InvoiceID": primary key that links an invoice header to its lines.  
• SALES_INVOICES."CustomerID": identifies the customer that owns the invoice.  
• SALES_INVOICELINES."InvoiceID": foreign‑key needed to join to SALES_INVOICES.  
• SALES_INVOICELINES."ExtendedPrice": the line amount that must be summed to obtain invoice totals (or directly summed per customer‑month).  

Typical filter / join conditions you will see in the queries  
• Join:  il."InvoiceID" = ih."InvoiceID"  
• Year restriction:  ih."InvoiceDate" LIKE '2014-%'  
• Month derivation:  SUBSTR(ih."InvoiceDate",1,7)  -- returns ‘YYYY‑MM’  

Below are ten Snowflake SQL snippets that move from quick inspections to the final median computation.  
(Each query is limited to 20 rows to keep the result sets manageable.)

```sql
-- 1) Distinct years present in SALES_INVOICES (quick sanity check)
SELECT DISTINCT SUBSTR("InvoiceDate",1,4) AS "Year"
FROM "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICES"
ORDER BY "Year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Distinct months for year 2014 (ensures every month exists)
SELECT DISTINCT SUBSTR("InvoiceDate",1,7) AS "Year_Month"
FROM "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICES"
WHERE "InvoiceDate" LIKE '2014-%'
ORDER BY "Year_Month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Sample of invoice headers from 2014
SELECT "InvoiceID",
       "CustomerID",
       "InvoiceDate"
FROM "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICES"
WHERE "InvoiceDate" LIKE '2014-%'
ORDER BY "InvoiceDate", "InvoiceID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Sample of invoice lines that belong to 2014 headers (join check)
SELECT il."InvoiceID",
       il."StockItemID",
       il."Quantity",
       il."ExtendedPrice"
FROM   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICELINES"  il
JOIN   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICES"      ih
       ON il."InvoiceID" = ih."InvoiceID"
WHERE  ih."InvoiceDate" LIKE '2014-%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Total amount per invoice (header level) for 2014
SELECT il."InvoiceID",
       SUM(il."ExtendedPrice") AS "Invoice_Total"
FROM   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICELINES"  il
JOIN   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICES"      ih
       ON il."InvoiceID" = ih."InvoiceID"
WHERE  ih."InvoiceDate" LIKE '2014-%'
GROUP BY il."InvoiceID"
ORDER BY il."InvoiceID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Monthly spend per customer for 2014
SELECT ih."CustomerID",
       SUBSTR(ih."InvoiceDate",1,7) AS "Year_Month",
       SUM(il."ExtendedPrice")      AS "Customer_Monthly_Spend"
FROM   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICELINES"  il
JOIN   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICES"      ih
       ON il."InvoiceID" = ih."InvoiceID"
WHERE  ih."InvoiceDate" LIKE '2014-%'
GROUP BY ih."CustomerID", SUBSTR(ih."InvoiceDate",1,7)
ORDER BY ih."CustomerID", "Year_Month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Average monthly spend per customer in 2014
WITH ctm AS (
  SELECT ih."CustomerID",
         SUBSTR(ih."InvoiceDate",1,7) AS "Year_Month",
         SUM(il."ExtendedPrice")      AS "Monthly_Spend"
  FROM   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICELINES" il
  JOIN   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICES"     ih
         ON il."InvoiceID" = ih."InvoiceID"
  WHERE  ih."InvoiceDate" LIKE '2014-%'
  GROUP BY ih."CustomerID", SUBSTR(ih."InvoiceDate",1,7)
)
SELECT "CustomerID",
       AVG("Monthly_Spend") AS "Avg_Monthly_Spend_2014"
FROM   ctm
GROUP BY "CustomerID"
ORDER BY "CustomerID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Distribution of the average monthly spends, sorted ascending
WITH ctm AS (
  SELECT ih."CustomerID",
         SUBSTR(ih."InvoiceDate",1,7) AS "Year_Month",
         SUM(il."ExtendedPrice") AS "Monthly_Spend"
  FROM   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICELINES" il
  JOIN   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICES"     ih
         ON il."InvoiceID" = ih."InvoiceID"
  WHERE  ih."InvoiceDate" LIKE '2014-%'
  GROUP BY ih."CustomerID", SUBSTR(ih."InvoiceDate",1,7)
)
SELECT AVG("Monthly_Spend") AS "Avg_Monthly_Spend_2014"
FROM   ctm
GROUP  BY "CustomerID"
ORDER  BY "Avg_Monthly_Spend_2014"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Exact median of the customer average monthly spend (PERCENTILE_CONT)
WITH ctm AS (
  SELECT ih."CustomerID",
         SUBSTR(ih."InvoiceDate",1,7) AS "Year_Month",
         SUM(il."ExtendedPrice") AS "Monthly_Spend"
  FROM   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICELINES" il
  JOIN   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICES"     ih
         ON il."InvoiceID" = ih."InvoiceID"
  WHERE  ih."InvoiceDate" LIKE '2014-%'
  GROUP BY ih."CustomerID", SUBSTR(ih."InvoiceDate",1,7)
),
cust_avg AS (
  SELECT "CustomerID",
         AVG("Monthly_Spend") AS "Avg_Monthly_Spend_2014"
  FROM   ctm
  GROUP BY "CustomerID"
)
SELECT PERCENTILE_CONT(0.5) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY "Avg_Monthly_Spend_2014") 
       AS "Median_Avg_Monthly_Spend_2014"
FROM   cust_avg
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Alternate median using MEDIAN window function (same result check)
WITH ctm AS (
  SELECT ih."CustomerID",
         SUBSTR(ih."InvoiceDate",1,7) AS "Year_Month",
         SUM(il."ExtendedPrice") AS "Monthly_Spend"
  FROM   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICELINES" il
  JOIN   "WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."WIDE_WORLD_IMPORTERS"."SALES_INVOICES"     ih
         ON il."InvoiceID" = ih."InvoiceID"
  WHERE  ih."InvoiceDate" LIKE '2014-%'
  GROUP BY ih."CustomerID", SUBSTR(ih."InvoiceDate",1,7)
),
cust_avg AS (
  SELECT "CustomerID",
         AVG("Monthly_Spend") AS "Avg_Monthly_Spend_2014"
  FROM   ctm
  GROUP BY "CustomerID"
)
SELECT MEDIAN("Avg_Monthly_Spend_2014") 
       OVER () AS "Median_Avg_Monthly_Spend_2014"
FROM   cust_avg
LIMIT 20;
```
